    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2506.10067v2"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper studies stochastic measurement-and-feedback control of quantum chaotic dynamics, focusing on the quantum Arnold cat map and an inverted harmonic oscillator (IHO) effective model. It derives a sequence of control probabilities p_n_star for order-n quantum operators, given by p_n_star = (e^{n kappa} - 1)/(e^{n kappa} - e^{-n gamma}), where kappa and gamma are positive strengths of the chaotic and control channels. The extraction focuses on this exact quantum operator threshold formula and its derivation.",
